Example output: `Final score: 10`', 'score = 10
print("Final score:", score
', 'score = 10
print("Final score:", score)
', 'script', NULL, 'Every opening bracket - `(`, `[`, `{` - needs a matching closing one. Python keeps reading, looking for that match, until it runs out of file, which is why the error can point somewhere that looks far away from the real mistake.', 'Count brackets in pairs on any line you''re not sure about. An editor that highlights matching brackets (like this one) makes this easy to check at a glance.', NULL, 'published', '6275f982a653c9a139676f50f1ea85e541e123691e9e385b452148cd7aeed9a2', NOW());
