Example: `classify(5)` should return `"positive"`.', 'def classify(n):
    if n > 0:
	x = "positive"
        return x
    return "non-positive"
', 'def classify(n):
    if n > 0:
        return "positive"
    return "non-positive"
', 'function', 'classify', 'Tabs and spaces can look identical on screen but mean different things to Python''s parser. Mixing them within the same block is ambiguous enough that Python refuses to guess and raises an error instead.', 'Set your editor to show whitespace characters, or just always use spaces (most Python style guides, and this editor, default to this).', NULL, 'published', 'fea6ef16cca2d8419ba02269d1ab155be29ebab9947318b0986db19a205e6bfc', NOW());
