Example output: `Ada`', 'name = "Ada"
Print(name)
', 'name = "Ada"
print(name)
', 'script', NULL, 'Python treats `Print`, `print` and `PRINT` as three unrelated names. Built-in functions and keywords are always lowercase, so a capital letter here means Python goes looking for a name that was never created.', 'If a `NameError` names something that looks like a familiar built-in, check its capitalisation first.', NULL, 'published', '500f0b10e6b98e5454a109d7680842bdf76d2a6d07535d53632bbd35bdeeca32', NOW());
INSERT INTO bh_puzzle_tests (puzzle_id, sort_order, label, args_py, kwargs_py, stdin_text, expect_kind, expect_py, compare_mode, is_hidden) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM bh_puzzles WHERE slug = 'capital-offence'), 1, 'prints the name', NULL, NULL, '', 'stdout', '"Ada\\n"', 'exact', 0);
