Example: `greet("Ada")` should return `"Hello, Ada"`.', 'def greet(greeting="Hello", name):
    return greeting + ", " + name
', 'def greet(name, greeting="Hello"):
    return greeting + ", " + name
', 'function', 'greet', 'Default parameter values have to come after every parameter that doesn''t have one - otherwise Python couldn''t tell which arguments you meant to skip.', 'When a function definition has default values, check they all sit at the end of the parameter list.', NULL, 'published', '4c2e85ea8f951017050913897e8e7f07a1c30d179090592704abe447e8d7660b', NOW());
