Example output: `Year 12`', 'class = "Year 12"
print(class)
', 'class_name = "Year 12"
print(class_name)
', 'script', NULL, 'Python''s keywords (`if`, `for`, `class`, `return`, and so on) are reserved - they always mean the same special thing, so they can never double up as a variable name.', 'If a `SyntaxError` points at a variable name that looks like an ordinary English word, check it isn''t one of Python''s keywords.', NULL, 'published', '80f105f086e78052008004dc516b7f0f1549192083f7ed153d5c4f4f158a2b27', NOW());
