Example: `check(5)` should return `"positive"`.', 'def check(n):
    if n > 0:
        result = "positive"
    else:
    result = "non-positive"
    return result
', 'def check(n):
    if n > 0:
        result = "positive"
    else:
        result = "non-positive"
    return result
', 'function', 'check', 'An `else:` needs its own indented body, lined up the same way as the `if` block''s body - it''s easy to fix the header and forget the line underneath.', 'Check the indentation of the line immediately under `else:`, not just the `else:` line itself.', NULL, 'published', '0903e446baa6999db3d26775711e91abdd423a4bbdebd5cc15a3aa24d543df83', NOW());
