Example: `classify_temp(35)` should return `"hot"`.', 'def classify_temp(celsius):
    if celsius > 30:
        return "mild"
    else:
        return "hot"
', 'def classify_temp(celsius):
    if celsius > 30:
        return "hot"
    else:
        return "mild"
', 'function', 'classify_temp', 'A condition can be perfectly correct while the two outcomes attached to it are swapped - the code still runs without error, it just confidently returns the opposite answer to the one you meant.', 'When a condition looks right but results seem backwards, check which branch returns which value, not just the comparison itself.', NULL, 'published', 'c6f7d8c115f37200749b7ae162252fd653599eba36c1d9f6a8d8d45a2dabdcb3', NOW());
