    return [n for n in numbers if n % 2 == 1]
', 'function', 'odd_only', 'A list comprehension''s filter condition is just an ordinary boolean expression - it is exactly as easy to get backwards here as in a regular `if` statement.', 'Read a comprehension''s `if` condition exactly as carefully as you would a normal `if` statement - it is easy to skim past.', NULL, 'published', '4d64cd7aa8d1cf37b8e2664c6be4a0d91055917c514a4a51dbedc81c8cca0767', NOW());
